DFlash verify: apply the batch's precomputed penalties (SGLang nightly-cu134-20260909-708f51e, speculative/dflash_utils.py).

Under overlap scheduling (the default) SamplingBatchInfo.copy_for_forward precomputes the penalties as
acc_additive_penalties (presence, frequency) and acc_scaling_penalties (repetition) and drops the orchestrator.
apply_dflash_verify_logits_adjustments still looked for the older name acc_linear_penalties, found nothing, and
applied no penalty to any verify row: with ./start-dflash.sh every presence/frequency/repetition penalty was a
no-op. This reads the current names, applies the repetition scaling over the block too (as
apply_scaling_penalties does), and without overlap takes both from the live penalizers.
Needs 0002 (the penalizers must see the generated tokens). Verified: greedy presence_penalty 0 vs 1.5 differ under
DFlash, the server default equals an explicit 1.5, tool calls and reasoning unaffected.

